tangular stack with diagonals/folds, text column lines. Cat atop sleeping, body oval ~160x70, head to left, tail curl. Ensure newspaper shows below cat.\n\nCould maybe table at x=240..960 y=570. Table front view. Background window left x=80..330, table and beam.\n\nWindow on left: tall multi-pane, maybe y=140..450, x=80..310. Beam from window diagonally across wall and table. But window behind table on left; sunlight enters. Add sunlit patch on floor at lower left and across tabletop. Sunbeams: two big translucent polygons crossing from window to table. Use muted yellow. Could use linear gradient with transparent fade. Flat vector maybe no blur. We'll do polygons with low opacity and a clip maybe. A good effect: clip light rays to wall? Simpler shapes crossing wall, tabletop; semi-transparent. Make sure rays don't obscure text. Could tone.\n\nBackground: wall maybe #e7dbc3. Add subtle horizontal trim at y=520? wallpaper dots? Keep simple. Perhaps a framed simple botanical print? But not requested; might distract. A hanging plant? Small kitchen table context. Use window plus a simple shelf? Hmm. Need rich composition but not clutter. Add a low wainscot maybe with muted terracotta #c9a88b? Or avoid. Let's create a warm mustard-tinged wall with simple vertical paneling lines in the lower section, floor at y=760. But table legs. Window left tall. Maybe add pair of subtle wall tiles? Keep minimal.\n\nLight from left: long diagonal beams from window (x~300, y~200) to lower-right. Add patch of sunlight on wall/table. Use `mix-blend-mode`? perhaps not. Just translucent #f6dca2.\n\nNeed detailed vector. Let's inspect if there are special requirements unknown? likely just evaluate visual. Need produce robust SVG. Might also render to PNG to inspect. Use rsvg-convert. Need maybe use fonts installed. Check."}
