ould illuminate left sides and cast shadows right. We can add warm highlight along left edges. Simpler: background beams behind objects; tabletop light patch on top of table with low opacity overlay, objects cast shadows to right.\n\nCould put sun rays behind table under table? Tabletop casts shadow. Fine.\n\nTable:\n- Table top y=585 maybe. Top includes elliptical perspective? Seen from front slightly above. To fit items and cat, top surface depth maybe 80 px: back edge at y=565, front edge y=635? Small table with full perspective. Front view of table front edge and top, all objects sit around y=520-600. Actually if front view at eye level, tabletop edge horizontal, but we need items resting. Flat illustration often slight top-down showing an oval tabletop. \"seen from the front\" means table full front with legs. We can use curved tabletop ellipse top to show surface. That's still front view. Need avoid weird. A rectangular table with slight perspective: top as polygon with back edge at y=545 (x=280..920) and front edge at y=600 (x=250..950), rounded. Legs at x=295 and x=875 from y=590 to 815, slightly tapered; cross-brace? Small table. Place items behind front edge but on top. Back edge y=545. Apples y~520? Hmm if tabletop surface from 545 to 600, items can be drawn with bases around 565-590. Cat/newspaper need more depth, so paper perspective extends from y=500 to 575; cat top around 455. Objects then extend up above top. That's fine. Table appears fairly low in canvas. Window behind.\n\nMaybe table top at y=600 with front edge. Table top surface as rounded rectangle from x=230 y=555 w=740 h=90 in a trapezoid? Use path M260 555 Q600 540 940 555 L970 635 Q600 655 230 635 Z. Top fill wood, front edge band from y=620 to 650. Legs from x=300 and x=870 y=640 to 830. Add apron (front rail) y=640..675. No chairs? small kitchen table maybe add chair on right? But cat and table objects enough. Window left. Could add simple chair back behind table on right? Would clutter.